hypotheses.statement:
There are positive integers $p_0\mid p$, depending only on $n$, with the following property. Let $f:X\to Z$ be a contraction of normal projective complex varieties, where $\dim X=n$, $\dim Z>0$, $X$ is klt, and $K_X$ is rationally linearly equivalent to the pullback of a rational Cartier divisor on $Z$. Then there are a rational function $\psi\in\mathbb C(X)^*$ and canonical bundle formula data satisfying the equality of rational divisors $$\label{eq:den-exact}
 K_X+\frac{1}{p_0}\mathop{\mathrm{div}}(\psi)=f^*D_Z,
 \qquad D_Z=K_Z+B_Z+M_Z.$$ Here $B_Z\geq0$ has coefficients in a rational DCC set depending only on $n$, the generalized pair $(Z,B_Z+M_Z)$ is generalized klt, and the moduli b-divisor $\mathbf M$ is b-nef with $p\mathbf M$ b-Cartier.

Assume $I_j$ for $j<n$. There are constants $C_n,c_n>0$ with the following property. Let $V$ be a normal projective canonical $n$-fold with $K_V\sim_{\mathbb Q}0$, and let a finite group $G$ act on $V$. Suppose that every $G$-equivariant rational fibration with geometrically integral generic fibre and positive-dimensional base and fibre has general-type smooth geometric generic fibre. If $P$ is an ample rational Cartier divisor with $g^*P\sim_{\mathbb Q}P$ for every $g\in G$, then $$\label{eq:scalar-estimates}
       \gamma(P;V)\le C_n(P^n)^{1/n},
       \qquad \varepsilon(P)\ge c_n(P^n)^{1/n}.$$ The constants are independent of $V$, $G$, and the denominator of $P$.

Let $Z$ be projective, $\mathbb Q$-factorial and klt of dimension $d\ge2$, and let $N$ be big, nef and semiample. Suppose that $d+1$ positive rational numbers with consecutive spacing $\Delta>0$ lie strictly between $(N^d)^{1/d}$ and $\gamma(N;Z)$. Then there is a covering family of integral subvarieties $S$ of dimension $0<e<d$ whose smooth geometric generic resolution $S^*$ satisfies $$\begin{aligned}
 N^eS&\le(2/\Delta)^{d-e}N^d,\label{eq:tracking-degree}\\
 K_{S^*}(N|_{S^*})^{e-1}
 &\le\bigl(K_Z+(2d/\Delta)N\bigr)|_S(N|_S)^{e-1}.
 \label{eq:tracking-canonical}
\end{aligned}$$ In addition, if a projective variety has a smooth model with nonnegative Kodaira dimension, then a smooth projective model of the geometric generic member of any covering family of integral subvarieties has nonnegative Kodaira dimension. The same statement holds with “general type” in place of “nonnegative Kodaira dimension.”

Fix $1\le e<n$ and $C'>0$. Let $(W_i,L_i)$ be a sequence of smooth projective $e$-folds with $\kappa(W_i)\ge0$ and big, nef, semiample rational Cartier divisors $L_i$, such that $$\label{eq:small-volume-hypotheses}
                  L_i^e\longrightarrow0,
                  \qquad K_{W_i}L_i^{e-1}\le C'L_i^e.$$ Assume $I_e$. After a subsequence and resolution of the Iitaka fibrations, their smooth geometric generic fibres $U_i$ have fixed positive dimension, satisfy $\kappa(U_i)=0$, and obey $$\label{eq:small-fibre-volume}
                     \mathop{\mathrm{vol}}(K_{U_i}+L_i|_{U_i})\longrightarrow0.$$ The restricted polarizations are big, nef and semiample. If the Iitaka base is a point, $U_i$ denotes the entire smooth model.

Let $V$ be a normal projective canonical complex variety of dimension $n\ge2$, with $K_V\sim_{\mathbb Q}0$ and canonical index $r$. Let $\pi:Y\to V$ be its canonical cyclic cover. Suppose that $L$ is an ample rational Cartier divisor and $C_1>0$ is rational, with $$1\le L^n\le2,\qquad \gamma(L;V)\le C_1.$$ Choose a positive rational number $b_0$ such that $$\label{eq:diag-b0}
 3(2b_0)^n<\frac14,\qquad b_0(C_1+1)<\frac34.$$ For every integer $t\ge2$, set $$Z_t=Y^t/\mu_{r,\mathrm{diag}},\qquad
 \theta_t:Z_t\longrightarrow V^t,\qquad
 P_t=\theta_t^*L^{\boxplus t}.$$ Then $P_t$ is ample and $$\label{eq:diag-epsilon}
 \varepsilon(P_t)\le\frac{(n+1)t^2}{b_0}.$$

